    "title": "Coachella 2026: First look at Sabrina Carpenter’s Pit Stop pop-up with Airbnb",
    "text": "Sabrina Carpenter is giving her fans an opportunity to take a pit stop between her headliner performances at the Coachella Valley Music and Arts Festival. The pop star has partnered with Airbnb for Sabrina’s Pit Stop, a pop-up event happening through Sunday, April 12, at 82338 Highway 111 in Indio. The pop-up is all Carpenter’s vision and may or may not be a hint of new things to come from the pop star. The pit stop is also full of easter eggs and hidden gems, including the Pretty Girl cleanup crew van featured in the music video for “House Tour,” which featured cameos from Margaret Qualley and Madelyn Cline. ALSO SEE: Sabrina Carpenter surprises fans at LA show with Christina Aguilera duet The pop-up has plenty of photo ops, including ones with vintage cars. Inside the pit stop, fans can “refuel” with some sweet slushie concoctions. Plus, those who attend the event can get some Sabrina-inspired merch. The event, which started Friday, is open to the public from 11 a.m.-1 p.m. and 4-8 p.m. Saturday, April 11 and concludes on Sunday, April 12, from noon until 3 p.m. Additionally, fans can prebook experience spots on Saturday, April 11, from 2.-3 p.m. and Sunday, April 12 from 11 a.m. to noon. Slushy’s available for attendees at Sabrina Carpenter’s Pit Stop pop-up event with Airbnb in Indio. (Carolyn Burt, SCNG) 1 of 14Slushy’s available for attendees at Sabrina Carpenter’s Pit Stop pop-up event with Airbnb in Indio. (Carolyn Burt, SCNG) Expand This year marks Carpenter’s second time performing at the annual music festival. The last time she performed was in 2024, where she performed her single that year, “Espresso,” live for the first time. The pop star also used that performance to tease her next single by having her friends in the audience hold up a sign that said: “Please, please, please perform ‘Espresso.’ ” Related: Sabrina Carpenter performs new song ‘Espresso’ at Coachella 2024 Since then, Carpenter has released two new albums, “Short n’ Sweet” and “Man’s Best Friend.” Additionally, in 2025, she won two Grammy Awards: best pop vocal album for “Short n’ Sweet” and best pop solo performance for “Espresso.” Carpenter will be performing again on the Coachella main stage on April 17 with her set scheduled to start at 9:05 p.m. It will also be live-streamed on YouTube. Things To Do: Let us help you plan your adventures with stories on events, entertainment and culture near you.By signing up, you agree to our Terms of Use, Privacy Policy, and to receive emails from The Press-Enterprise.",
